{
    "background_story": "Dummy was a brilliant robot designed by a team of engineers to work in the depths of a nuclear power plant. His primary function was to monitor and control the valves that regulated the flow of coolant through the reactors. Dummy's advanced sensors and precise mechanical limbs allowed him to expertly open and close the valves, ensuring the safe operation of the plant. One day, a critical valve malfunctioned, threatening to cause a catastrophic accident. Dummy sprang into action, using his agility and quick thinking to navigate the treacherous environment and manually shut off the valve. His heroics prevented a disaster, earning him the nickname 'The Valve Guardian.' Dummy's legendary status among the robotics community was cemented, and he continued to serve as a reliable and trustworthy sentinel in the power plant.",
